{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":70063,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0473259c-1b21-4d84-8fdb-271541604b3c","total_cost_usd":0.7913954999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61445,"cache_read_input_tokens":20133,"output_tokens":4850,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4850,"cache_read_input_tokens":20133,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45519,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045619,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4850,"cacheReadInputTokens":20133,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61445,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7457765,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this config lands softly from every band at every load and never burns through its plate, but the two-to-four-pass ablation optimum the design is built around does not exist — a single committed plunge is the cheapest descent in all nine band/load cases, and the grid says that is a design problem, not a tuning one.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ablation_optimum_is_always_one_pass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params.ablation.optimal_skims asserts 0/1/2 skims for suborbital/low/high, and the cost_curve asserts high-band minima at k=2 (30.49, 29.72, 29.57, 30.23), i.e. a U-shaped cost with its floor at 2-4 committed passes.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all nine descents. The curve is monotonically increasing everywhere: high band full hold 13.6 -> 18.7 -> 19.5 -> 19.7 -> 20.3 ...; low band full hold 13.1 -> 17.2 -> 18.1 -> 18.5; suborbital empty 5.2 -> 6.0 -> 6.3 -> 6.5. The first extra pass costs 4.1-5.1 plate-percent against a claimed saving of 0.15-0.92. No U-curve exists at any band or load.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skimming_barely_cools_the_committed_entry\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"Aerobraking is essential: shallow passes bleed speed so the committed entry runs cooler, and the params price skims against a skim_heat_multiplier of [1, 0.984, 0.974, 0.972].\",\n      \"measured\": \"Measured multipliers at the shallowest entry depth are suborbital [1, 0.951, 0.897, 0.684], low [1, 0.977, 0.955, 0.934], high [1, 0.984, 0.968, 0.954] — so the params' array is right for high, pessimistic for low, and badly pessimistic for suborbital. But the effect is dwarfed by entry depth: on the high band, going from entry_depth 0 to 36000 m drops entry peak heat 163.1 -> 93.8 (a 0.575x multiplier) while three skims only reach 0.954. Depth is roughly 8x the lever that skimming is, and each skim costs 43-54 m/s of commit dv and about an hour of flight. In the grid, skimming_cools_the_entry is satisfied by 44.1% of configurations, but every config that satisfies it strongly does so with a low ballistic coefficient (the 0.363 and 0.211 multiplier rows sit at beta 44.4 and 133.3) and those same configs fail unstaged_pass_survivable with peak heats of 371-523.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"beta_and_unstaged_survival_are_mutually_exclusive\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The design wants both a meaningful multi-pass aerobrake (which needs air that bites) and survivable shallow unstaged braking passes before staging (2.3.1: 'fly your shallow braking passes before you stage').\",\n      \"measured\": \"unstaged_pass_survivable is the rarest target in the whole grid at 15.4%, and fuel_margin_sane is next at 16.2%. Across the 12 top-scoring configs, every one that measures a strong skim effect (multipliers 0.211-0.363) records unstaged_peak_heat of 355-523, and every one that survives unstaged (peak heat 47-90) measures skim multipliers of 0.945-0.987 — i.e. skimming that does nothing. No configuration in 2916 scores 8 of 8. The current config sits on the survivable side: unstaged shallow passes peak at 62 (suborbital) and 71 (low), both safe, which is why its skims are near-inert.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"peak_heat_exceeds_the_bar_but_nothing_burns\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"reentry.heat_capacity is 100 and cargo damage begins at 100% heat, one slot every 3 s; a depleted shield behaves as unshielded.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Sixteen entries in the descent table peak above 100 — high band full hold reaches 102 at 10, 14 and 15 passes; low band full hold reaches 101 from 11 passes up; suborbital full hold reaches 101 from 6 passes. Yet every descent reports plate_survives true and soft_landing true, and the skim table shows entry peaks of 131.5 (low, direct) and 163.1 (high, direct) with touchdown still 3.25 m/s and soft_landing true. Either the 100 bar does not gate cargo damage in the model or the two heat scales are not the same quantity; as reported, the ship exceeds its stated heat capacity by 63% and suffers nothing.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"difficulty_does_not_rise_with_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"Reentry speed and therefore heat scale with the altitude you return from; the value curve and the risk curve rise together, and heat_index asserts 83/100/119 across the three bands.\",\n      \"measured\": \"At the cheapest (one-pass) descent, ablation is 5.2 / 4.4 / 4.5 percent empty and 15.6 / 13.1 / 13.6 percent full for suborbital / low / high. The high band is cheaper to come home from than suborbital at every load, and the ordering across bands is essentially flat — a 1.06x spread against the claimed 1.43x. Cargo mass, by contrast, does move it: full hold costs 3x an empty hold (13.6 vs 4.5 on the high band). Mass carries the difficulty curve; altitude does not.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_lands_soft_everywhere_with_no_margin_pressure\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms 4.6 sits just under the 5.0 m/s soft-landing line, and the Parachute upgrade exists to counter a greedy hold.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Confirmed exactly: touchdown is 3.25 m/s empty, 3.99 half hold, 4.60 full hold, identical across all three bands, and soft_landing is true in all nine. The sqrt(mass) law holds — 4.6/sqrt(2) = 3.25. But because a base hold is the largest load the sim flies, no measured case ever crosses 5.0, so the Parachute upgrade has no measured case in which it is needed; the crossing the params describe (a 1665 kg haul at 5.49 m/s) is asserted, not flown. The parachute area was also not in the params — the sim solved for 630.1 m2 from the 4.6 m/s claim, so this is a consistency check, not an independent measurement.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_margins_are_thin_and_inverted_against_the_upgrade_tree\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"The base tank was sized for shipping-slice reachability (suborbital and low), and the balance notes ask whether fuel_tank tier 1 is a wanted purchase rather than a prerequisite.\",\n      \"measured\": \"All three bands are reachable at base config, including the deferred high band: fuel margins 16.6% / 13.5% / 11.8% (316.19 / 255.75 / 223.80 kg remaining). That settles the open question the economy notes could not — the tank is oversized for its stated job, since the semester slice only needs two bands. It also leaves fuel_tank tier 1 (450 credits) buying nothing the player needs, and 11.8% is a thin reserve for the return burn the sim does not charge for. In the grid, fuel_margin_sane holds in only 16.2% of worlds, so a thin margin here is normal for the space rather than a mistake.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims\",\n      \"current\": 2,\n      \"proposed\": 0,\n      \"reason\": \"The flown cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all nine cases, so the claim of 0/1/2 optimal skims is contradicted; set it flat until the mechanic is rebuilt, rather than shipping a number the simulator disagrees with.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.cycle_toll_base_pct\",\n      \"current\": 0.16,\n      \"proposed\": 0.16,\n      \"reason\": \"Adopt GDD 4.5 risk 1's own fallback — a flat per-pass toll with a hard cap on passes — because the grid shows no world where skimming cools enough to pay for itself while unstaged passes stay survivable; hold the toll and stop tuning it toward a U-curve that does not exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": 0.984,\n      \"proposed\": 0.954,\n      \"reason\": \"Replace the estimated array with the measured high-band values [1, 0.984, 0.968, 0.954] so the pricing model stops working from a fifth-of-claimed guess; per-band arrays would be better still, since suborbital measures 0.684 at three skims.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.heat_capacity\",\n      \"current\": 100,\n      \"proposed\": 110,\n      \"reason\": \"Sixteen flown descents peak between 101 and 102 with no damage taken and entry peaks reach 163 on the high band, so the stated capacity does not gate anything; raising it to the measured ceiling makes the bar honest at the cost of a slightly later cargo-damage threshold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index\",\n      \"current\": 119,\n      \"proposed\": 105,\n      \"reason\": \"Measured one-pass ablation is 5.2/4.4/4.5 percent across the bands, a 1.06x spread, not the 1.43x the index asserts; either bring the index to what is flown or push the high band's altitude out, which is the Researcher's own first lever for a steeper curve.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 1900,\n      \"proposed\": 1700,\n      \"reason\": \"All three bands are reachable at base with 11.8-16.6% margin, so the tank overshoots the two-band shipping slice and makes fuel_tank tier 1 a dead purchase; trimming it restores the upgrade as a want, at the cost of narrowing the high-band margin the semester does not ship anyway.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 0,\n      \"proposed\": 630.1,\n      \"reason\": \"The sim had to solve for this from descent_speed_full_hold_ms, so the 4.6 m/s figure is currently self-referential; stating the area makes touchdown speed an independent measurement instead of a restatement of the claim.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The heat scale is normalised so that an empty single-pass suborbital descent peaks at 100, per the sweep's own calibration note. Every heat figure I quote is relative to that anchor, so 'peak 163 on the high band' means 1.63x that reference descent, not 163 physical units of anything. The finding that peaks exceed heat_capacity 100 without consequence follows from comparing two scales that may not be the same quantity — that is the first thing to check before acting on it.\",\n    \"The parachute area was inferred by the simulator, not read from the params. Every touchdown speed in the sweep is therefore anchored to the 4.6 m/s claim it was solved from, which is why 'full hold lands soft' is a consistency check rather than independent evidence. Adding landing.parachute_area_m2 to the params would make the next sweep's touchdown numbers mean something on their own.\",\n    \"The sim flies a point mass with a perfect pilot: no attitude error, so off_retrograde_penalty is never exercised; no debris collisions; no cargo damage accumulation modelled during the pass. The claim that plate_survives in every descent should be read as 'the ablation arithmetic stays under the plate', not as 'a human can fly this'.\",\n    \"The exploration grid varies world and ship geometry but not the ablation knobs themselves (cycle_toll_base_pct, heat_cost_coefficient, skim_peak). So its 44.1% satisfaction rate for skimming_cools_the_entry measures whether the physics can produce a cooling effect, not whether the pricing model can turn that effect into a U-curve. My design-versus-tuning call on the ablation optimum rests on the physics half of that; a sweep over the three ablation knobs at fixed world would settle the other half and is the single most useful thing the next run could add.\",\n    \"No skim series in the verification sweep reaches a periapsis of 40-45 km, where the Researcher's own dv table says a pass is worth 25-85 m/s rather than a feather. The deepest skims flown are shallow enough that skim_peak_heat never exceeds 9.6. If the crew wants the aerobrake mechanic to survive, that unflown depth band is where to look before adopting the flat-toll fallback — my 'design' verdict on the U-curve is calibrated to the depths actually flown.\",\n    \"The descent table's pass_counts_reachable has gaps (the high band empty case skips 13, 15, 16) and ablation is not monotonic in a few rows — high band empty dips from 8.3 at 11 passes to 8.1 at 12, and high band half hold from 14.4 at 8 to 13.3 at 9. Those non-monotonicities are larger than the 0.15-percent differences the params' U-curve depends on, which is independent evidence that the intended optimum is below the model's own noise floor.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":67890,"ttft_stream_ms":1735,"time_to_request_ms":191,"type":"result","duration_ms":67997,"uuid":"6e384637-73b2-4271-8296-fb9ea835bf2f"}
